<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.handback.returns ~ handback ~ the one return every fire runs

`lares spirit handback <pet>[#<n>]` names exactly one return: `file=<path|->`, `text=<words>`, or `record= <uri>[@<hash>]` (a record already landed, read through the door first). A report lands as residue under the pet's own name, once per key (`key=`, else the instance's tag, else the words alone). The record stands first; then, where a summons edge names the instance, the edge names the record and the coordinator's lane frees (`mandate= <uri>@<hash>` names which edge). A hand-back no edge answers lands all the same; only a line naming its mandate refuses there, and its record stays.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ report · record

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`report` params=`pet/ferry-read#1 file/- ~ the report on stdin lands and the edge closes`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`record` params=`pet/ferry-read#1 record/lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/x ~ name a record already landed`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ face · pet · file · text · record · key · mandate

<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/face`>>

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`pet` params=`takes/pet-or-tag needs/required seat/1 as/<pet> ~ the one who returns: a pet, or <pet>#<n> for one instance`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`file` params=`takes/host-path ~ the report from a host file, or - for stdin`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`text` params=`takes/words ~ the report as words`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`record` params=`takes/ref ~ a landed record as <lar uri>[@<hash>]`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`key` params=`takes/key ~ the idempotency key`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`mandate` params=`takes/ref ~ the mandate whose edge this hand-back answers, <uri>@<hash>`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ocap/write-on-the-daemon-wiki ~ a harness hook and a hand type the same line; the tiddler door gates each write`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · spirit-pet-malformed · handback-unknown · handback-moved · summons-unknown · summons-ambiguous · spirit-secret-shaped · spirit-write-refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[face.handback.returns pet/ferry-read file/-]] ~ no return, two returns, or a malformed record, instance or mandate`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`spirit-pet-malformed` params=`cure/[[face.handback.returns pet/ferry-read file/-]] ~ the word reads as no pet name`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`handback-unknown` params=`cure/[[face.handback.returns pet/ferry-read file/-]] ~ no record stands at the uri named`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`handback-moved` params=`~ the record reads another hash than the line names`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`summons-unknown` params=`~ no edge answers the instance under the mandate named; the record stays`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`summons-ambiguous` params=`~ several edges name the instance; name the mandate`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`spirit-secret-shaped` params=`~ the words hold secret-shaped strings`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`spirit-write-refused` params=`~ the tiddler door answered no put`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

